hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24101","Bahz narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rifaah ibn Shaddad, he said: I used to stand at the head of al-Mukhtar, and when his lying became clear to me I intended, by Allah, to draw my sword and strike his neck, until I remembered a hadith Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever grants a man security for his life then kills him will be given the banner of treachery on the Day of Resurrection."
"24102","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Isa al-Qari Abu Umar narrated to us, al-Suddi narrated to me, from Rifaah al-Qitbani, he said: I entered upon al-Mukhtar, he said, and he threw a cushion for me and said: Were it not that my brother Jibril stood up from this I would have cast it to you. He said: So I wanted to strike his neck, then I remembered a hadith my brother Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whichever believer grants a believer security for his blood then kills him, I am free of the killer."
